; spell.clay — PROCESS + BOUNDARY clusters: the renderer wire.
; STATUS: contract stub. Blocked by the EDN data reader (BOUNDARY) and
; ergonomically by BUG-002 (nested receive) — see spell/README.md.
;
; The renderer is a dumb terminal for UI trees. This namespace owns the
; whole relationship: spawn, handshake, frames out, events in, and the
; async command surface. It knows the protocol and nothing about the
; app's state; it knows Port mechanics and nothing about clay.
;
; ── Wire protocol (verbatim from clayd; any renderer must speak it) ──
;
; COMMANDS IN (harness → renderer, one EDN value per line):
;   {:cmd :frame :tree <tree>}         layout + render; emits :tree-warnings
;   {:cmd :screenshot :path "..."}     render to texture, save PNG, ack
;   {:cmd :clipboard-put :text "..."}  set system clipboard
;   {:cmd :clipboard-get}              async reply {:event :clipboard ...}
;   {:cmd :inject :event <ev>}         synthetic input, re-emitted as event
;   {:cmd :scroll-state :id "..."}     async reply {:event :scroll-state ...}
;   {:cmd :wheel :dy N :x px :y py}    synthetic wheel at position
;   {:cmd :quit}                       deliberate shutdown, emits :quit
;
; EVENTS OUT (renderer → harness):
;   {:event :ready}                    handshake
;   {:event :tick}                     heartbeat ~0.5s
;   {:event :mouse-down :x N :y N :button 1 :id "..." :text-index I}
;   {:event :mouse-up :x N :y N :button 1 :id "..."}
;   {:event :text-input :text "s"}     real keystroke only
;   {:event :key :key "name" :ctrl b :shift b}
;   {:event :resize :w N :h N}
;   {:event :clipboard :text "..." :truncated b}
;   {:event :scroll-state :id "..." :y N :overflow N :content-h N
;          :viewport-h N :at-bottom b}
;   {:event :tree-warnings :warnings [...] :deduped b}
;   {:event :screenshot :path "..."} / {:event :wheel-applied}
;   {:event :eof} / {:event :quit}
;
; ── Contract (the public fns this namespace will export) ─────────────
;
; (start!) → {:ok port} | {:error reason}
;   Port.open {:spawn_executable, clayd-path} with [{:line, 65536},
;   :binary, :exit_status]; await {:event :ready} bounded by 15s of
;   MONOTONIC time (not line count — a spammy renderer must not starve
;   the handshake). SPELL_HEADLESS=1 passes --hidden.
;   No quitting? atom, no respawn! here: crash-vs-quit is :transient
;   restart in the SUPERVISOR (main.bl), not state in this namespace.
;
; (frame! port tree) → :ok
;   spell.ui/realize the tree, spell.store/tap! :frame-log, pr-str,
;   Port command. The tap is the test surface — tests assert at the
;   wire, never at app internals.
;
; (next-event port) → {:ok event-map} | :eof | {:unreadable line}
;   Block in receive for the port's line, read-data it (BOUNDARY —
;   never eval). Port messages are {port, {:data, {:eol, line}}}:
;   depth 3, so until BUG-002 lands the destructure is an
;   erlang/element chain behind one helper.
;
; (clipboard-put! port text) (clipboard-get! port) (screenshot! port path)
; (scroll-state! port id) (wheel! port dy) (quit! port)
;   One send-line each, async replies arrive as events. clipboard-put!
;   also taps :clipboard-writes.
;
; Renderers: clayd (C++, vendored, unchanged — the reference), a pure
; beam-lisp ANSI terminal renderer (planned; proves the protocol is
; renderer-agnostic), or any future drop-in (Odin/Zig — deferred, the
; wire makes them interchangeable).

(ns spell.clay)
